## Complexity

Let `m` be the number of meetings and `n` be the number of rooms.

### Time Complexity

```text
O(m log m + m log n)
```

* Sorting meetings: `O(m log m)`
* Each meeting performs heap operations: `O(log n)`

### Space Complexity

```text
O(m + n)
```

The meetings and the two heaps require additional memory.

---

## Key Takeaway

The important idea is to maintain **two priority queues**:

```text
Available Rooms
      ↓
Smallest room number
```

and

```text
Busy Rooms
      ↓
Earliest finishing meeting
```

This allows us to efficiently simulate the scheduling rules while always choosing the correct room.

> **Greedy Strategy:** At every meeting, choose the smallest available room. If no room is available, delay the meeting until the earliest room becomes free.
